{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3262","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3262","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3262\",\"parent_revision\":\"eee6acfdd0af24e1d970336222f7f9f0184a9650242d97126bcc2c3b832b8bdb\",\"root_revision\":\"eee6acfdd0af24e1d970336222f7f9f0184a9650242d97126bcc2c3b832b8bdb\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Refactor\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-28\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nThe `WorkItemBackend` protocol (`plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/backend_types.py:118-134`) is the generic work-item surface every backend must implement \u2014 GitHub, Beads, SQLite, and Memory alike \u2014 and its own docstring states this explicitly (\\\"Generic work-item surface every backend must implement... No PyGithub.Repository parameter, no GraphQL-only primitives\\\"). Despite that, several of its mandatory methods are named after GitHub specifically: `try_get_github`, `close_github_issue`, `resolve_github_issue`, `fetch_open_issues_by_title`, `fetch_github_issue_body`, `view_enrich_from_github`, and a parameter `issue_to_local_fields(issue: IssueNode)`.\\n\\nThis is the same class of problem already fixed elsewhere in this pass (docstrings/prose naming GitHub for behavior actually gated on the generic `SyncProvider`/`ContentProvider` protocols) \u2014 but here the GitHub-specific wording is in the method names themselves, on a protocol every non-GitHub backend must also implement. A reader (human or agent) encountering `Beads`'s or `SQLite`'s implementation of `close_github_issue` has no way to tell from the name alone that this is the generic \\\"close a work item\\\" operation, not a GitHub-only capability.\\n\\nObserved scope: a repo-wide grep found the affected method names referenced across roughly 37 files, of which approximately 25 contain string-based test mocks (e.g. `mocker.patch(\\\"...try_get_github\\\")`) that would need updating in lockstep with any rename \u2014 a blind rename risks breaking those mocks silently since they match by string, not by import.\\n\\nSuggested replacement names (not verified against every call site): `try_get_remote`, `close_work_item`, `resolve_work_item`, `fetch_open_work_items_by_title`, `fetch_work_item_body`, `view_enrich`.\\n\\nThis item was deliberately not fixed as part of the tightening pass that found it \u2014 the blast radius was judged too large to verify safely without running the full test suite as part of that same pass.\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: work-backlog-item skill tightening pass, backend-language-leak sweep, 2026-08-28\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-08-28\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"933df68fd819805cbd4eb7258e3cac7d1c1b671ea06496b74c875d7a9dbc5c70\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABRP6-QQ\"}"}